A||||5||Fformula88||Mounting Borla Exhaust||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||12-28-2000||07:12 PM||||To anyone that has a Borla exhaust... how did you mount it to the car?  By the pics I have seen it does not look like it has the mounting brackets attached to it.  Do they have to be added?  Or did you mount it another way?  <P>If you had brackets added to the exhaust, were they welded on?  I am concerned that the welds could cause the exhaust system to rust, or at least the brakcets to rust and drop the exhaust off the car.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-28-2000||07:33 PM||||The systems come with brackets that are also made out of stainless steel.  The brackets are mounted in different locations depending on what year/model you have......that is why they weren't attached initially.  Once you determine exactly where the brackets need to go have a muffler shop weld them in place.  As long  as they use stainless rod it won't rust out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||12-28-2000||07:58 PM||||I cut the original mounts off my stock exhaust system and had a welder weld them onto my Borla system with stainless steel welding rods. The brackets are 409 stainless steel so they will surface rust but won't rust through.<P>See pictures.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Img_0154.jpg">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Img_0156.jpg">   <P><BR>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 12-28-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 12-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||12-28-2000||08:25 PM||||When I replace my exhaust with the Borla system, I also replaced the cat.  The Borla was hung from the new cat pipe and hung by the two rear hangers by the exhaust tips.  I saved my old hangers, but the muffler shop didn't have the stainless rod for the weld.  One of the rear hanger brackes did break, but that was just rewelded.||||reg||3
Z||000004||Fformula88||12-29-2000||10:12 AM||||Thanks for the info and the pics everyone.  I am currently debating whether to get the Borla exhaust, but am probably going to get it.<P>My next ? is on the tips.  Did you guys put different tips on the system?  or did you order it with tips on it?  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroparts.com||12-29-2000||11:17 AM||||The ones listed above all got the tips on the units. You can use the org. tips if you want but it is much cheaper to get the tips<BR>on the system! <P>thanks tim||||reg||14
